From 0861654f97441d280960ff3a1757773aa49064be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:56:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Wi-Fi: ARP only for the gateway, RX records with their
 FCS and W_RXLEN_CROP, a probe of DraStic's W_IF store;
 0.4.0-beta.2-rocknixds.2

Three things a review against melonDS and the DS hardware found before any device run:
- wfcnet answered ARP requests for any address, the DS's own included: a DHCP client that probes its offered
  lease (RFC 2131 4.4.1) would have declined it. It answers for the gateway only; the host test covers the probe.
- The RX record held the frame without its FCS and reported that length, and W_RXLEN_CROP (0x0DA) was never read.
  The record now holds the whole frame as the hardware stores it, and the header's length takes off what the
  crop register says ((crop << 1) & 0x1FE for plain frames, (crop >> 7) & 0x1FE for WEP ones; the firmware's
  0x0602 crops the 4-byte FCS), so a stack that sets the crop differently still sees the right length.
- The hook assumed DraStic's stock 16-bit store keeps a written W_IF as is. The layout check now probes that
  (0x5a5a through the stock handler, read back) and logs "IF store plain" or "write-1-to-clear"; in the latter
  case the flags go straight into the register memory, so a set is never turned into a clear.
VERSION 0.4.0-beta.2-rocknixds.2: the shader output patch plus the Wi-Fi path (off unless configured).
Still untested on a handheld.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EHHmyacNZtyRhmxZoUYRa8
